[
  {
    "sha": "9cdc9116e97e0542d0ccdf0140801a97bda52d0a",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDljZGM5MTE2ZTk3ZTA1NDJkMGNjZGYwMTQwODAxYTk3YmRhNTJkMGE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-24T06:26:27Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-24T06:26:27Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): read the fig8 part wall as one wall, and try the edge route before a pass-link lift\n\nThe ring set split the boundary of the cutter-centre area into ring 0 and\nthe walls with a side tolerance of 1 um, below the 5 um flats of the round\njoins. On fig8 two 0.117 mm stretches of the part wall read as the stock\nside: Inside left two gaps in its wall ring, and Outside cut the two\nstretches first, each reached by a lift over the part and a plunge into\nmaterial. SIDE_EPS is now 10 um, twice the flattening error.\n\nThe pass link round a part now tries the edge route (the walk of the\nplanner's join) after the straight chord, each chord with the same proof,\nbefore it lifts. A lift keeps the straight chord's reason.\n\nfig8: Inside 6 -> 0 lifts, Outside 12 -> 3 (each named); no lift over the\npart, no plunge into material; flute_reach rapid findings 9 -> 3.\n\nFixes #3824\nFixes #3825\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
